From 7d8007792c6ee0e9902f45809a114e8b13c10145 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:02:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] refactor(retrieval-server): render every PDF with Typst,
 remove x2p_v1

Plan 5.2, last step: after the canary, Typst is the only PDF renderer.

- generate_pdf: the xhtml2pdf path is gone (the python-markdown front end,
  the D8 pre-pass, the raw-HTML allowlist, the 50-row table chunker, the
  status-emoji map, the _CSS stylesheet with its footer frame and the
  xhtml2pdf log capture), and with it the 1.14 "shows as boxes" note, the
  script route and pdf_charsets. RENDERERS is ("typst",) and render_job
  renders every job with Typst, so a job or request still naming "x2p_v1",
  or anything unknown, renders with it. Every request gets the Typst tool
  description. The caps and the line-based table-row count, filename
  sanitizing, source sidecars, page counts, the locale and letterhead
  options and the stats reporting are unchanged.
- pdf_renderer: the valid values are ("typst",). PDF_RENDERER is still
  read; an old value (x2p_v1, or anything else) is ignored with one warning
  per process, as are the obsolete PDF_RENDERER_CANARY,
  PDF_RENDERER_CANARY_CUSTOMERS and PDF_RENDERER_SCRIPT_ROUTE. The renderer
  stays pinned per turn, and a request or recovered durable run pinned to
  x2p_v1 renders with Typst. pdf_script_route leaves the request models,
  the graph state, sub-agent state and the tool runtime: stored run input
  that still carries it validates (the models ignore undeclared keys), and
  LangGraph ignores the dropped key in an old checkpoint.
- pdf_worker and pdf_render_child: no warm child any more. Every render and
  every parse runs in a one-shot child that is reaped when its job ends, and
  a child that never receives its job exits after 60 s. --selftest renders
  with Typst and extracts and rasterizes the result with PDFium; the parse
  ops are unchanged. PDF_RENDER_RLIMIT_MB and the PDF_WORKER_* recycling
  settings are gone, and app shutdown has no warm child left to stop.
- pdf_metrics labels every render renderer="typst".

Tests: the x2p-only tests (D8 pre-pass, the raw-HTML allowlist on
python-markdown, the emoji map, the charset tables, the x2p parity baselines
under tests/fixtures/pdf/x2p_baseline, xhtml2pdf log capture, the x2p OOM)
are removed. What still matters is tested on Typst: placeholders printed
verbatim, no network fetch, lists and tables right after a paragraph line,
caps, filenames, sidecars, the revise flow, the worker's timeout, OOM, busy
and one-shot semantics, log isolation of the Typst child, requests and
recovered runs pinned to x2p_v1 rendering with Typst, and a fresh server
process (app, graph modules, one render, one parse) that loads nothing of
the removed renderer.

